# DTF tier manifest: image-inspect-repository-scope
# (artifact-keeper#5096, PR #5098; artifact-keeper#5111, PR #5112)
# Profile-set: s3 / single. One MinIO bucket shared by every repository: OCI
# manifests and blobs are digest-keyed there, not namespaced per repository, so
# the object behind another repository's digest is readable under any key. A
# filesystem stack is rooted per repository and cannot show the cross-repository
# half of either bug.
#
# THE BUGS
#   #5096  GET /api/v1/repositories/{key}/image-inspect and
#          .../image-builds/base-info resolved a tag through oci_tags, but
#          returned a sha256: reference unchanged and read it by digest. A digest
#          of another repository, or of another image in the same repository,
#          was described under the requested repository and image.
#   #5111  The config and provenance blobs a resolved manifest names were read
#          by digest without asking whether the repository records them. A
#          manifest pushed into a repository can name any blob digest.
#
# SETUP: a private repository holding team/app and an index, a public repository
# holding team/app, other/thing and manifests that borrow the private content.
# Reads of the public repository are anonymous: that is who the bug exposed the
# private content to. Every image carries a marker in its config and every
# refusal is also checked for the private marker.
#
#   (FIX #5096) on the public repository:
#     - the private image's digest, a private index child's digest, and an index
#       pushed there that lists the private child: 404, the digest case
#       byte-identical (hex masked) to a digest that exists nowhere, no private
#       marker; base-info `found: false`.
#     - a digest of other/thing under team/app, and the other way round: 404.
#     - a platform child under another image name: 404.
#   (FIX #5111) on the public repository:
#     - a manifest naming the private config: 404 by tag and digest, identical
#       (hex masked) to a manifest naming a config stored nowhere, no private
#       marker; base-info `found: false`.
#     - an attested index whose provenance blob is the private repository's: 200
#       without provenance and without the private Dockerfile.
#   (CONTROL) both images: tag and digest of the public image, an index by tag
#       and by digest and its platform child, a provenance blob the repository
#       records (Dockerfile returned), the private image through the admin on its
#       own repository, an absent digest 404, base-info `found: true`.
#
# RED on 1.11.10: every FIX case above answers 200 / `found: true` with the
# other repository's or image's config. GREEN on 1.11.11.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: not under test, about 60 requests in a burst.
PROFILES="storage.s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
